WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.455
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.755 --> 00:00:09.013
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.313 --> 00:00:16.668
Unit thirty-six: Prepositions of Movement. Today you will describe how people and things move from place to place.

4
00:00:16.968 --> 00:00:19.585
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.533 --> 00:00:23.638
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.483 --> 00:00:25.368
To.

7
00:00:26.383 --> 00:00:27.942
To means toward a place.

8
00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:29.783
I go to school.

9
00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:32.525
Your turn. Say: To.

10
00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:36.170
To.

11
00:00:36.917 --> 00:00:37.569
From.

12
00:00:38.583 --> 00:00:40.548
From means starting at a place.

13
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:42.592
She comes from Siem Reap.

14
00:00:43.183 --> 00:00:45.696
Your turn. Say: From.

15
00:00:48.533 --> 00:00:49.244
From.

16
00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:50.833
Into.

17
00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:53.803
Into means moving inside.

18
00:00:54.417 --> 00:00:55.905
He walked into the room.

19
00:00:56.517 --> 00:00:58.844
Your turn. Say: Into.

20
00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:02.446
Into.

21
00:01:03.183 --> 00:01:03.975
Out of.

22
00:01:04.983 --> 00:01:07.598
Out of means moving from inside to outside.

23
00:01:08.183 --> 00:01:09.579
She ran out of the house.

24
00:01:10.183 --> 00:01:12.186
Your turn. Say: Out of.

25
00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:15.814
Out of.

26
00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:17.679
Across.

27
00:01:18.683 --> 00:01:20.985
Across means from one side to the other.

28
00:01:21.583 --> 00:01:23.420
We walk across the bridge.

29
00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:26.506
Your turn. Say: Across.

30
00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:30.623
Across.

31
00:01:31.383 --> 00:01:32.071
Through.

32
00:01:33.083 --> 00:01:35.791
Through means from one end to the other inside something.

33
00:01:36.383 --> 00:01:38.116
The train goes through a tunnel.

34
00:01:38.717 --> 00:01:41.555
Your turn. Say: Through.

35
00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:45.064
Through.

36
00:01:45.817 --> 00:01:46.481
Up.

37
00:01:47.483 --> 00:01:49.471
Up means to a higher place.

38
00:01:50.083 --> 00:01:51.735
She climbs up the stairs.

39
00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:54.468
Your turn. Say: Up.

40
00:01:57.333 --> 00:01:57.998
Up.

41
00:01:58.750 --> 00:01:59.612
Down.

42
00:02:00.617 --> 00:02:02.326
Down means to a lower place.

43
00:02:02.917 --> 00:02:04.312
He walks down the hill.

44
00:02:04.917 --> 00:02:07.755
Your turn. Say: Down.

45
00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:11.357
Down.

46
00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:15.748
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:19.897
Visal, how do you get to school? Describe your journey.

48
00:02:20.983 --> 00:02:27.351
I walk to school, across the bridge and through the park. These words show movement from one place to another.

49
00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:30.531
What is the difference between in and into?

50
00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:40.982
In shows a place: The boy is in the room. Into shows movement: The boy walked into the room. Out of is the opposite: He ran out of the room.

51
00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:43.386
And up and down?

52
00:02:44.483 --> 00:02:57.712
Up goes to a higher place and down goes to a lower place: She climbs up the stairs and walks down the hill. To and from show direction: from home to school.

53
00:02:58.867 --> 00:03:00.646
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:01.483 --> 00:03:04.377
Grammar focus: Prepositions of movement.

55
00:03:04.677 --> 00:03:05.864
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:08.503
I walk to school every day.

57
00:03:09.417 --> 00:03:11.114
The boy ran into the room.

58
00:03:12.017 --> 00:03:13.587
We walk across the bridge.

59
00:03:14.533 --> 00:03:21.330
Use to, from, into, out of, across, through, up and down with movement verbs. In shows a place, but into shows movement.

60
00:03:22.083 --> 00:03:24.910
Be careful! Don't say: He walked in the room.

61
00:03:26.867 --> 00:03:28.820
Say: He walked into the room.

62
00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.119
Use into for movement inside.

63
00:03:31.933 --> 00:03:34.377
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:36.261
My Journey.

65
00:03:36.561 --> 00:03:39.152
I walk from my house to school every morning.

66
00:03:40.167 --> 00:03:43.269
First I go across the bridge, and then I walk through the park.

67
00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:46.754
I go up the stairs and into my classroom.

68
00:03:47.767 --> 00:03:50.486
After school I walk out of the gate and down the road.

69
00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.685
The way to my school is short and safe.

70
00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:59.162
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:00.017 --> 00:04:02.959
She walked blank the room. (movement inside)

72
00:04:03.259 --> 00:04:06.506
A, in. B, into. C, at.

73
00:04:10.067 --> 00:04:12.055
The answer is B: into.

74
00:04:13.217 --> 00:04:16.403
We walk blank the bridge. (one side to the other)

75
00:04:16.703 --> 00:04:19.869
A, across. B, up. C, from.

76
00:04:23.433 --> 00:04:25.642
The answer is A: across.

77
00:04:26.783 --> 00:04:29.993
He ran blank the house. (inside to outside)

78
00:04:30.293 --> 00:04:33.679
A, into. B, out of. C, through.

79
00:04:37.233 --> 00:04:39.256
The answer is B: out of.

80
00:04:40.417 --> 00:04:41.998
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:42.298 --> 00:04:49.423
A, He goes in the school every day.. B, He goes to school every day.. C, He goes at school every day..

82
00:04:52.967 --> 00:04:56.034
The answer is B: He goes to school every day..

83
00:04:57.183 --> 00:05:00.297
According to the reading, where does the writer walk through?

84
00:05:00.597 --> 00:05:04.274
A, the park. B, the bridge. C, the stairs.

85
00:05:07.833 --> 00:05:09.380
The answer is A: the park.

86
00:05:10.567 --> 00:05:13.544
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:14.383 --> 00:05:17.660
Describe your journey to school using two prepositions of movement.

88
00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:27.997
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:28.297 --> 00:05:40.867
I walk from my house across the bridge and through a small park. Then I go into the school gate and up the stairs to my classroom. I use across, through, into and up to describe my journey.

90
00:05:41.167 --> 00:05:42.899
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:43.783 --> 00:05:47.910
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and prepositions of movement.

92
00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:51.942
Today's value is safety. Be careful near cars and roads.

93
00:05:52.242 --> 00:05:55.022
See you in Unit thirty-seven. Goodbye!

94
00:05:55.322 --> 00:05:58.636
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

